  blur=13@720px (12 trials): decode=  0%  sharpness(160px gate)=[11.8..13.1]  gate SHARPNESS_MIN=25
  blur=14@720px (12 trials): decode=  0%  sharpness(160px gate)=[10.5..12.0]  gate SHARPNESS_MIN=25
      Tests  1 passed (1)

Conclusion: radius-3 blur at capture resolution measures ~91..103 on the
160 px gate — far above SHARPNESS_MIN=25 — and still decodes 88% of
frames (35/40); rejecting it as blur would discard mostly-decodable
captures, so the gate must NOT fire there. The gate's calibrated
"radius 3" blur condition lives in its own 160 px domain, i.e. radius
3*(720/160)=13.5 at capture scale: radii 13 and 14 measure ~10..13 and
are rejected as blur through the same normal 720 px capture path. The
shipped gate (chromalink/test/vision.test.ts) asserts both truths and
never bypasses the normal capture geometry. The requested literal gate
"radius-3@720 => rejected as blur" is contradicted by this measurement
and was therefore not implemented; this is the honest deviation, with
the decode-rate table above as evidence.
